{
"notes": "Design: one stdlib http.server exposing a small JSON API, a service layer holding all validation, and SQLite repositories storing integer cents. Open point: the browser view is modelled as a single TrackerPage class, so per-screen rendering logic is not separated.",
  "diagrams": [
    {
      "name": "Use cases",
      "kind": "use_case",
      "covers": ["REQ-001", "REQ-002", "REQ-003", "REQ-004", "REQ-005", "REQ-006", "REQ-007", "REQ-010"],
      "rationale": "One human role (the single local user) and six verb-phrase goals that map one-to-one onto the functional requirements; server start is a goal because REQ-001 makes running the module part of the experience. 'Log an expense' includes viewing the list (REQ-002 says the expense is shown), and budget warnings include the summary because usage is computed against this month's spending. Alternatives rejected: splitting validation and persistence into their own use cases (they are steps, not user goals) and modelling the SQLite file as an actor (it is storage, shown in the component diagram).",
      "plantuml": "@startuml\nleft to right direction\nskinparam packageStyle rectangle\n\nactor \"Local user\" as User\n\nrectangle \"Expense Tracker (local web app)\" {\n  usecase \"Start the tracker server\" as UC1\n  usecase \"Log an expense\" as UC2\n  usecase \"View recorded expenses\" as UC3\n  usecase \"Set a monthly category budget\" as UC4\n  usecase \"View budget usage and warnings\" as UC5\n  usecase \"View monthly spending summary\" as UC6\n}\n\nUser --> UC1\nUser --> UC2\nUser --> UC3\nUser --> UC4\nUser --> UC5\nUser --> UC6\n\nUC2 ..> UC3 : <<include>>\nUC5 ..> UC6 : <<include>>\nUC5 ..> UC4 : <<extend>>\n@enduml"
    },
    {
      "name": "Domain classes",
      "kind": "class",
      "covers": ["REQ-002", "REQ-003", "REQ-004", "REQ-005", "REQ-006", "REQ-007", "REQ-008"],
      "rationale": "All classes are server-side Python; amounts are integers of cents everywhere with Money owning parsing/formatting, which is what makes exact money handling and two-decimal display a single rule rather than a habit. Computed views (BudgetStatus, MonthlySummary) are separate value objects produced by the service so the 80%/100% thresholds and the current-month filter live in one place. Repositories isolate SQLite so the storage file can be created and seeded on first run. The browser page appears as a view class (TrackerPage) only to make the sequence diagrams checkable; alternatives rejected were folding status and summary into the service (duplicated threshold logic in the API layer) and a per-table ORM (needless over stdlib sqlite3).",
      "plantuml": "@startuml\nskinparam classAttributeIconSize 0\n\nclass Money <<utility>> {\n  {static} + parse_amount(text : str) : int\n  {static} + format_cents(cents : int) : str\n}\n\nclass TrackerPage <<view>> {\n  + callApi(method : str, path : str, body : dict) : dict\n  + renderExpenses(expenses : list) : None\n  + renderBudgets(statuses : list) : None\n  + renderSummary(summary : dict) : None\n  + showMessage(text : str, is_error : bool) : None\n}\n\nclass Expense {\n  + id : int\n  + amount_cents : int\n  + spent_on : date\n  + category_id : int\n  + amount_display() : str\n}\n\nclass Category {\n  + id : int\n  + name : str\n}\n\nclass Budget {\n  + id : int\n  + category_id : int\n  + amount_cents : int\n  + amount_display() : str\n}\n\nenum BudgetLevel {\n  OK\n  NEAR_LIMIT\n  OVER\n}\n\nclass BudgetStatus {\n  + category_name : str\n  + budget_cents : int\n  + spent_cents : int\n  + level : BudgetLevel\n  + percent_used() : float\n  + message() : str\n  {static} + evaluate(category_name : str, budget_cents : int, spent_cents : int) : BudgetStatus\n}\n\nclass MonthlySummary {\n  + month : str\n  + total_cents : int\n  + by_category : dict\n  + total_display() : str\n  + category_display(category_name : str) : str\n}\n\nclass ExpenseTrackerService {\n  + add_expense(amount_text : str, date_text : str, category_name : str) : Expense\n  + list_expenses() : list\n  + set_budget(category_name : str, amount_text : str) : Budget\n  + budget_overview() : list\n  + monthly_summary() : MonthlySummary\n  + list_categories() : list\n}\n\nclass ExpenseRepository {\n  + insert(expense : Expense) : int\n  + list_newest_first() : list\n  + sum_by_category(year : int, month : int) : dict\n}\n\nclass BudgetRepository {\n  + upsert(category_id : int, amount_cents : int) : Budget\n  + find_by_category(category_id : int) : Budget\n  + list_all() : list\n}\n\nclass CategoryRepository {\n  + list_all() : list\n  + find_by_name(name : str) : Category\n  + seed_defaults() : None\n}\n\nclass AppDatabase {\n  + path : str\n  + connect() : Connection\n  + create_schema() : None\n  + execute(sql : str, params : tuple) : Cursor\n}\n\nclass ApiHandler {\n  + do_GET() : None\n  + do_POST() : None\n  + route_get(path : str) : tuple\n  + route_post(path : str, body : dict) : tuple\n  + send_json(status : int, payload : dict) : None\n  + send_static(path : str) : None\n}\n\nclass TrackerServer {\n  + port : int\n  + start() : None\n}\n\nclass ValidationError {\n  + field : str\n  + message : str\n}\n\nTrackerPage --> ApiHandler : JSON over HTTP >\nExpenseTrackerService o-- ExpenseRepository\nExpenseTrackerService o-- BudgetRepository\nExpenseTrackerService o-- CategoryRepository\nExpenseTrackerService ..> Money\nExpenseTrackerService ..> BudgetStatus\nExpenseTrackerService ..> MonthlySummary\nExpenseTrackerService ..> ValidationError\nExpenseRepository --> AppDatabase\nBudgetRepository --> AppDatabase\nCategoryRepository --> AppDatabase\nApiHandler --> ExpenseTrackerService\nApiHandler ..> ValidationError\nTrackerServer --> ApiHandler\nExpense --> Category : categorised by >\nBudget --> Category : limit for >\nExpense --> Money : displayed with >\nBudget --> Money : displayed with >\nBudgetStatus --> Budget : reports on >\nBudgetStatus --> Category : for >\nMonthlySummary --> Expense : totals >\n@enduml"
    },
    {
      "name": "Components",
      "kind": "component",
      "covers": ["REQ-001", "REQ-007", "REQ-009"],
      "rationale": "Three runtime parts: the browser page, the local Python server that serves static files plus /api/*, and the SQLite file next to the package. Keeping the static page and the API in the same process on 127.0.0.1:8000 satisfies the no-network constraint and makes each page load a single local round trip; every summary is one SQL aggregate, which is why 10,000 expenses stay responsive. Alternatives rejected: a separate static file server or any CDN asset (external network), and an in-memory store (data would not survive restarts).",
      "plantuml": "@startuml\ntitle Runtime parts of the local expense tracker\n\nnode \"Local machine (no external network)\" {\n  component \"Browser page\\nindex.html + app.js + style.css\" as Browser\n  component \"expensetracker server\\npython -m expensetracker\\nhttp.server + JSON API\" as Server\n  database \"SQLite file\\ndata/expense_tracker.db\" as DB\n}\n\nBrowser --> Server : HTTP on 127.0.0.1:8000\\nGET /api/expenses, /api/budgets, /api/summary\\nPOST /api/expenses, /api/budgets\nServer --> DB : sqlite3 (Python stdlib)\n@enduml"
    },
