      "rationale": "Warnings are derived, never stored: the service lists budgets, asks the repository for this month's per-category sums, and lets BudgetStatus decide OK / NEAR_LIMIT / OVER at 80% and 100%. Computing the level in one value object keeps the threshold definition (an assumption, not a user setting) in a single place and lets the repository do the summation in SQL. Alternatives rejected: persisting a warning flag on the budget row (stale as soon as an expense is added) and comparing percentages in JavaScript (thresholds would drift from the API contract).",
