      "role": "user",
      "content": "Approved design:\n[sequence] Budget overview:\n@startuml\nautonumber\ntitle View budget usage with warnings (REQ-004, REQ-005)\n\nparticipant TrackerPage\nparticipant ApiHandler\nparticipant ExpenseTrackerService\nparticipant Clock\nparticipant BudgetRepository\nparticipant ExpenseRepository\nparticipant CategoryRepository\nparticipant BudgetStatus\n\nTrackerPage -> ApiHandler : GET /api/budgets\nApiHandler -> ExpenseTrackerService : budget_overview()\nExpenseTrackerService -> Clock : current_month() = \"2026-05\"\nExpenseTrackerService -> BudgetRepository : list_all()\nBudgetRepository --> ExpenseTrackerService : [Budget(category_id=1, 10000), Budget(category_id=2, 5000)]\nExpenseTrackerService -> ExpenseRepository : sum_by_category(2026, 5)\nExpenseRepository --> ExpenseTrackerService : {1: 8500}\nExpenseTrackerService -> CategoryRepository : list_all()\nCategoryRepository --> ExpenseTrackerService : [Category(1, Groceries), Category(2, Transport)]\nExpenseTrackerService -> BudgetStatus : evaluate(\"Groceries\", 10000, 8500)\nBudgetStatus -> BudgetStatus : percent_used() = 85.0\nBudgetStatus --> ExpenseTrackerService : BudgetStatus(level=NEAR_LIMIT, spent_cents=8500)\nExpenseTrackerService -> BudgetStatus : evaluate(\"Transport\", 5000, 12000)\nBudgetStatus --> ExpenseTrackerService : BudgetStatus(level=OVER, spent_cents=12000)\nExpenseTrackerService --> ApiHandler : [BudgetStatus, BudgetStatus]\nApiHandler --> TrackerPage : 200 {budgets: [{category, budget_display, spent_display, percent, level, message}]}\nTrackerPage -> TrackerPage : renderBudgets(), showMessage(\"85% of budget used\")\n\nnote over BudgetStatus\nlevel = OK below 80%, NEAR_LIMIT from 80% up to 100%,\nOVER above 100% of the category budget (REQ-005).\nend note\n@enduml\n\n\n[component] Components:\n@startuml\ntitle Runtime parts of the local expense tracker\n\nnode \"Local machine (no external network)\" {\n  component \"Browser page\\nindex.html + app.js + style.css\" as Browser\n  component \"expensetracker server\\npython -m expensetracker\\nhttp.server.HTTPServer + JSON API\" as Server\n  database \"SQLite file\\ndata/expense_tracker.db\" as DB\n}\n\nBrowser --> Server : HTTP on 127.0.0.1:8000\\nGET /api/expenses, /api/categories, /api/budgets, /api/summary\\nPOST /api/expenses, /api/budgets\nServer --> DB : sqlite3 (Python stdlib), one connection per call\n\nnote right of Server\n  Single-threaded http.server.HTTPServer (not ThreadingHTTPServer).\n  On start-up the SQLite file and schema are created if missing, the\n  seven fixed categories are seeded, then requests are served (REQ-001, REQ-007).\nend note\n\nnote bottom of DB\n  Amounts are stored as integer cents; each repository call opens its own\n  short-lived connection, so no locking is needed (REQ-008, REQ-009).\nend note\n@enduml\n\n\n[class] Domain classes:\n@startuml\nskinparam classAttributeIconSize 0\ntitle Domain and runtime classes\n\nclass App <<entry>> {\n  {static} + main() : None\n}\n\nclass Money <<utility>> {\n  {static} + parse_amount(text : str) : int\n  {static} + format_cents(cents : int) : str\n}\n\nclass Dates <<utility>> {\n  {static} + parse_date(text : str) : date\n}\n\nclass Clock <<utility>> {\n  + today() : date\n  + current_month() : str\n}\n\nclass TrackerPage <<view>> {\n  + callApi(method : str, path : str, body : dict) : dict\n  + renderExpenses(expenses : list) : None\n  + insertRow(expense : dict) : None\n  + renderBudgets(statuses : list) : None\n  + renderSummary(summary : dict) : None\n  + showMessage(text : str, is_error : bool) : None\n}\n\nclass Expense {\n  + id : int\n  + amount_cents : int\n  + spent_on : date\n  + category_id : int\n  + amount_display() : str\n}\n\nclass Category {\n  + id : int\n  + name : str\n}\n\nclass Budget {\n  + id : int\n  + category_id : int\n  + amount_cents : int\n  + amount_display() : str\n}\n\nenum BudgetLevel {\n  OK\n  NEAR_LIMIT\n  OVER\n}\n\nclass BudgetStatus {\n  + category_name : str\n  + budget_cents : int\n  + spent_cents : int\n  + level : BudgetLevel\n  + percent_used() : float\n  + message() : str\n  {static} + evaluate(category_name : str, budget_cents : int, spent_cents : int) : BudgetStatus\n}\n\nclass MonthlySummary {\n  + month : str\n  + total_cents : int\n  + by_category : dict\n  + total_display() : str\n  + category_display(category_name : str) : str\n}\n\nclass ExpenseTrackerService {\n  - clock : Clock\n  + add_expense(amount_text : str, date_text : str, category_name : str) : Expense\n  + list_expenses() : list\n  + set_budget(category_name : str, amount_text : str) : Budget\n  + budget_overview(month : str = None) : list\n  + monthly_summary(month : str = None) : MonthlySummary\n  + list_categories() : list\n}\n\nclass ExpenseRepository {\n  + insert(expense : Expense) : int\n  + list_newest_first() : list\n  + sum_by_category(year : int, month : int) : dict\n}\n\nclass BudgetRepository {\n  + upsert(category_id : int, amount_cents : int) : Budget\n  + find_by_category(category_id : int) : Budget\n  + list_all() : list\n}\n\nclass CategoryRepository {\n  + list_all() : list\n  + find_by_name(name : str) : Category\n  + seed_defaults() : None\n}\n\nclass AppDatabase {\n  + path : str\n  + create_schema() : None\n  + connect() : Connection\n  + execute(sql : str, params : tuple) : int\n  + fetchall(sql : str, params : tuple) : list\n}\n\nclass ApiHandler {\n  + do_GET() : None\n  + do_POST() : None\n  + route_get(path : str) : tuple\n  + route_post(path : str, body : dict) : tuple\n  + send_json(status : int, payload : dict) : None\n  + send_static(path : str) : None\n}\n\nclass TrackerServer {\n  + port : int\n  + serve_forever() : None\n}\n\nclass ValidationError {\n  + field : str\n  + message : str\n}\n\nApp --> AppDatabase : creates\nApp --> ExpenseTrackerService : wires\nApp --> TrackerServer : starts\n\nTrackerPage --> ApiHandler : JSON over HTTP >\nExpenseTrackerService o-- ExpenseRepository\nExpenseTrackerService o-- BudgetRepository\nExpenseTrackerService o-- CategoryRepository\nExpenseTrackerService --> Clock : uses >\nExpenseTrackerService ..> Money\nExpenseTrackerService ..> Dates\nExpenseTrackerService ..> BudgetStatus\nExpenseTrackerService ..> MonthlySummary\nExpenseTrackerService ..> ValidationError\nExpenseRepository --> AppDatabase\nBudgetRepository --> AppDatabase\nCategoryRepository --> AppDatabase\nApiHandler --> ExpenseTrackerService\nApiHandler ..> ValidationError\nTrackerServer --> ApiHandler\nExpense --> Category : categorised by >\nBudget --> Category : limit for >\nExpense --> Money : displayed with >\nBudget --> Money : displayed with >\nBudgetStatus --> Budget : reports on >\nBudgetStatus --> Category : for >\nMonthlySummary --> Expense : totals >\n\nnote right of Money\n  parse_amount raises ValidationError(\"amount\", reason) for a missing,\n  non-numeric or non-positive amount; format_cents always prints two\n  decimals (REQ-002, REQ-008, REQ-010).\nend note\n\nnote right of Dates\n  parse_date raises ValidationError(\"date\", reason) unless the text is\n  a valid YYYY-MM-DD calendar date (REQ-002).\nend note\n\nnote bottom of AppDatabase\n  connect() opens one short-lived sqlite3 connection per call inside a\n  with block and closes it afterwards. The server is a single-threaded\n  HTTPServer, so no shared connection and no lock are needed; the file\n  is created on first run (REQ-007).\nend note\n\nnote bottom of ExpenseRepository\n  sum_by_category returns dict[int, int] keyed by category_id\n  (SELECT category_id, SUM(amount_cents) ... GROUP BY category_id);\n  the service joins the names from CategoryRepository (REQ-005, REQ-006).\nend note\n\nnote right of ExpenseTrackerService\n  month defaults to clock.current_month() when the caller passes None,\n  so a test can fix 2026-05 explicitly (REQ-005, REQ-006).\nend note\n@enduml\n\n\n[activity] Expense validation flow:\n@startuml\ntitle Validate and save an expense (REQ-002, REQ-010)\n\nstart\n:User submits amount, date, category;\n:Money.parse_amount(amount_text);\n:Dates.parse_date(date_text);\nif (amount missing, non-numeric or <= 0?) then (yes)\n  :ValidationError(\"amount\", reason);\n  :400 {field: \"amount\", message};\n  :Keep entered values in the form;\n  stop\nelse (no)\n  if (date not a valid calendar date?) then (yes)\n    :ValidationError(\"date\", reason);\n    :400 {field: \"date\", message};\n    :Keep entered values in the form;\n    stop\n  else (no)\n    if (category not in the fixed list?) then (yes)\n      :400 {field: \"category\", message};\n      :Keep entered values in the form;\n      stop\n    else (no)\n      :ExpenseRepository.insert(Expense with amount_cents);\n      :201 with the saved expense and its display strings;\n      :Insert the row at its date position and show \"Expense saved\";\n      stop\n    endif\n  endif\nendif\n@enduml\n\n\n[sequence] Log expense:\n@startuml\nautonumber\ntitle Load the list and log an expense (REQ-002, REQ-003, REQ-008, REQ-010)\n\nparticipant TrackerPage\nparticipant ApiHandler\nparticipant ExpenseTrackerService\nparticipant CategoryRepository\nparticipant ExpenseRepository\n\n== page load (REQ-003) ==\nTrackerPage -> ApiHandler : GET /api/expenses\nApiHandler -> ExpenseTrackerService : list_expenses()\nExpenseTrackerService -> ExpenseRepository : list_newest_first()\nExpenseRepository --> ExpenseTrackerService : [Expense(id=6), ...]\nExpenseTrackerService --> ApiHandler : list\nApiHandler --> TrackerPage : 200 {expenses: [...]}\nTrackerPage -> TrackerPage : renderExpenses()\n\n== submit the form (REQ-002) ==\nTrackerPage -> ApiHandler : POST /api/expenses {amount: \"12.50\", date: \"2026-05-03\", category: \"Groceries\"}\nApiHandler -> ExpenseTrackerService : add_expense(\"12.50\", \"2026-05-03\", \"Groceries\")\nExpenseTrackerService -> ExpenseTrackerService : Money.parse_amount(\"12.50\") = 1250\nExpenseTrackerService -> ExpenseTrackerService : Dates.parse_date(\"2026-05-03\")\nExpenseTrackerService -> CategoryRepository : find_by_name(\"Groceries\")\nCategoryRepository --> ExpenseTrackerService : Category(id=1, name=Groceries)\nExpenseTrackerService -> ExpenseRepository : insert(Expense(amount_cents=1250, spent_on=2026-05-03, category_id=1))\nExpenseRepository --> ExpenseTrackerService : 7\nExpenseTrackerService --> ApiHandler : Expense(id=7)\nApiHandler --> TrackerPage : 201 {id: 7, amount_display: \"12.50\", date: \"2026-05-03\", category: \"Groceries\"}\nTrackerPage -> TrackerPage : insertRow(...), showMessage(\"Expense saved\")\n\nnote over ApiHandler\nInvalid amount or date: Money.parse_amount / Dates.parse_date raise a\nValidationError, answered with 400 {field, message}. Nothing is inserted, the\npage keeps the entered values and the list is not refetched (REQ-002, REQ-010).\nend note\n@enduml\n\n\n[sequence] Monthly summary:\n@startuml\nautonumber\ntitle Monthly spending summary (REQ-006, REQ-008, REQ-009)\n\nparticipant TrackerPage\nparticipant ApiHandler\nparticipant ExpenseTrackerService\nparticipant Clock\nparticipant ExpenseRepository\nparticipant CategoryRepository\nparticipant MonthlySummary\n\nTrackerPage -> ApiHandler : GET /api/summary\nApiHandler -> ExpenseTrackerService : monthly_summary()\nExpenseTrackerService -> Clock : current_month() = \"2026-05\"\nExpenseTrackerService -> ExpenseRepository : sum_by_category(2026, 5)\nExpenseRepository --> ExpenseTrackerService : {1: 4000, 2: 6000}\nExpenseTrackerService -> CategoryRepository : list_all()\nCategoryRepository --> ExpenseTrackerService : [Category(1, Groceries), Category(2, Transport)]\nExpenseTrackerService -> MonthlySummary : by_category = {Groceries: 4000, Transport: 6000}, total_cents = 10000\nMonthlySummary --> ExpenseTrackerService : summary\nExpenseTrackerService -> MonthlySummary : total_display()\nMonthlySummary --> ExpenseTrackerService : \"100.00\"\nExpenseTrackerService -> MonthlySummary : category_display(\"Groceries\")\nMonthlySummary --> ExpenseTrackerService : \"40.00\"\nExpenseTrackerService --> ApiHandler : MonthlySummary(month=\"2026-05\")\nApiHandler --> TrackerPage : 200 {month, total_display: \"100.00\", categories: [{name, total_display}]}\nTrackerPage -> TrackerPage : renderSummary()\n\nnote over ExpenseRepository\nSUM(amount_cents) GROUP BY category_id, filtered by spent_on between the\nfirst and last day of the month; rows from other months are excluded by the\nquery. The service maps category_id to names (REQ-006, REQ-009).\nend note\n@enduml\n\n\n[sequence] Set budget:\n@startuml\nautonumber\ntitle Set or update a monthly budget (REQ-004)\n\nparticipant TrackerPage\nparticipant ApiHandler\nparticipant ExpenseTrackerService\nparticipant CategoryRepository\nparticipant BudgetRepository\n\nTrackerPage -> ApiHandler : POST /api/budgets {category: \"Groceries\", amount: \"350.00\"}\nApiHandler -> ExpenseTrackerService : set_budget(\"Groceries\", \"350.00\")\nExpenseTrackerService -> ExpenseTrackerService : Money.parse_amount(\"350.00\") = 35000\nExpenseTrackerService -> CategoryRepository : find_by_name(\"Groceries\")\nCategoryRepository --> ExpenseTrackerService : Category(id=1)\nExpenseTrackerService -> BudgetRepository : upsert(1, 35000)\nBudgetRepository --> ExpenseTrackerService : Budget(id=3, category_id=1, amount_cents=35000)\nExpenseTrackerService --> ApiHandler : Budget\nApiHandler --> TrackerPage : 200 {category: \"Groceries\", budget_display: \"350.00\"}\nTrackerPage -> TrackerPage : showMessage(\"Budget saved\"), update Groceries row\n\nnote over ApiHandler\nNegative, missing or non-numeric amount: Money.parse_amount raises\nValidationError, answered with 400 {field: \"amount\", message}; no budget\nrow is written (REQ-004, REQ-010).\nend note\n@enduml\n\n\n[sequence] Startup and storage:\n@startuml\nautonumber\ntitle Start-up, schema creation and recovery of stored data (REQ-001, REQ-007)\n\nparticipant App\nparticipant AppDatabase\nparticipant CategoryRepository\nparticipant ExpenseRepository\nparticipant BudgetRepository\nparticipant ExpenseTrackerService\nparticipant TrackerServer\n\nnote over App\npython -m expensetracker runs App.main(), which wires the parts below\nin this order and then serves the tracker page (REQ-001).\nend note\nApp -> AppDatabase : new AppDatabase(\"data/expense_tracker.db\")\nApp -> AppDatabase : create_schema()\nnote right of AppDatabase\n  sqlite3.connect() creates data/expense_tracker.db when the file is\n  missing, then CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS categories, expenses, budgets.\nend note\nAppDatabase --> App : schema ready\nApp -> CategoryRepository : new CategoryRepository(db)\nApp -> CategoryRepository : seed_defaults()\nnote right of CategoryRepository\n  Seeds Groceries, Rent, Transport, Utilities, Entertainment, Health and\n  Other only when the table is empty, so a restart keeps existing rows.\nend note\nApp -> ExpenseRepository : new ExpenseRepository(db)\nApp -> BudgetRepository : new BudgetRepository(db)\nApp -> ExpenseTrackerService : new ExpenseTrackerService(expenses, budgets, categories, Clock())\nApp -> TrackerServer : new TrackerServer(port=8000, handler=ApiHandler(service))\nApp -> TrackerServer : serve_forever()\nTrackerServer --> App : serving on 127.0.0.1:8000\n\nnote over TrackerServer\nSingle-threaded HTTPServer; every repository call opens its own short-lived\nsqlite3 connection, so expenses and budgets are simply re-read from the file\nafter a restart (REQ-007).\nend note\n@enduml\n\n\n[use_case] Use cases:\n@startuml\nleft to right direction\nskinparam packageStyle rectangle\n\nactor \"Local user\" as User\n\nrectangle \"Expense Tracker (local web app)\" {\n  usecase \"Start the tracker server\" as UC1\n  usecase \"Log an expense\" as UC2\n  usecase \"View recorded expenses\" as UC3\n  usecase \"Set a monthly category budget\" as UC4\n  usecase \"View budget usage and warnings\" as UC5\n  usecase \"View monthly spending summary\" as UC6\n}\n\nUser --> UC1\nUser --> UC2\nUser --> UC3\nUser --> UC4\nUser --> UC5\nUser --> UC6\n\nUC2 ..> UC3 : <<include>>\nUC5 ..> UC6 : <<include>>\nUC5 ..> UC4 : <<extend>>\n@enduml\n"
