    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Approved requirements:\n# Requirements\n\nA single-user personal expense tracker that runs in the browser, served locally by Python. It records expenses by amount, date and category, tracks monthly budgets per category with near-limit warnings, and shows monthly spending by category; data persists across restarts.\n\n## Functional requirements\n\n### REQ-001 Local web app served by Python (must)\n\nThe expense tracker runs in the browser as a web app served locally by `python -m expensetracker`. It uses only the Python 3.12 standard library and needs no network access beyond the local machine.\n\n- Given the app is not running, when the developer runs `python -m expensetracker`, then the server starts and the tracker page is reachable in a browser on the local machine.\n- Given the tracker page is open, when the user uses the app, then expenses, budgets and summaries are served by the local Python server without contacting any external service.\n\n### REQ-002 Log an expense (must)\n\nThe user can record an expense with an amount, a date and a category chosen from the available categories. The expense is saved and shown in the expense list.\n\n- Given the expense form, when the user submits amount 12.50, date 2026-05-03 and category Groceries, then the expense is saved and appears in the expense list.\n- Given the expense form, when the user submits a missing, non-numeric or non-positive amount, then an error message is shown and no expense is saved.\n- Given the expense form, when the user submits a date that is not a valid calendar date, then an error message is shown and no expense is saved.\n\n### REQ-003 View recorded expenses (must)\n\nThe app shows the recorded expenses in a list, newest first, each with its amount, date and category.\n\n- Given three saved expenses with different dates, when the expense list is displayed, then all three appear ordered by date from newest to oldest with amount, date and category shown.\n- Given no expenses have been saved, when the expense list is displayed, then an empty-state message is shown instead of an error.\n\n### REQ-004 Set a monthly budget per category (must)\n\nThe user can set or update a monthly spending budget for each category. The budget is stored and shown next to that category.\n\n- Given no budget exists for Groceries, when the user sets a budget of 300.00, then the budget is saved and displayed for Groceries.\n- Given a budget of 300.00 for Groceries, when the user changes it to 350.00, then the stored and displayed budget is 350.00 and the earlier value is no longer used.\n- Given the budget form, when the user enters a negative or non-numeric budget, then an error message is shown and no budget is saved.\n\n### REQ-005 Near-limit and over-limit budget warnings (must)\n\nFor each category with a budget, the app shows how much of the budget this month's spending has used and warns when spending reaches 80% of the limit, and flags the category as over budget when spending exceeds 100%.\n\n- Given a Groceries budget of 100.00 and 85.00 spent this month, when the budget view is shown, then Groceries is marked as close to its limit.\n- Given a Groceries budget of 100.00 and 120.00 spent this month, when the budget view is shown, then Groceries is marked as over budget.\n- Given a Groceries budget of 100.00 and 40.00 spent this month, when the budget view is shown, then Groceries is shown without a warning.\n\n### REQ-006 Monthly spending summary by category (must)\n\nThe app shows the total amount spent in the current calendar month and the same total broken down by category. Expenses from other months are excluded.\n\n- Given expenses of 40.00 in Groceries and 60.00 in Transport in the current month, when the summary is shown, then the monthly total is 100.00 with Groceries 40.00 and Transport 60.00.\n- Given an expense dated in a previous month, when the current month's summary is shown, then that expense is not included in the total or the category breakdown.\n\n### REQ-007 Data persists across restarts (must)\n\nExpenses and budgets are stored in a local SQLite database file so they are still available after the server is stopped and started again.\n\n- Given saved expenses and budgets, when the server is stopped and `python -m expensetracker` is started again, then all previously saved expenses and budgets are shown.\n- Given no database file exists, when the app starts for the first time, then it creates the storage file and starts with an empty expense list.\n\n## Non-functional requirements\n\n### REQ-008 Exact money handling (must)\n\nMonetary amounts are stored exactly, without floating-point rounding drift, and are displayed with two decimal places.\n\n- Given expenses of 0.10 and 0.20 in the same category, when the summary is shown, then the category total is displayed as 0.30.\n- Given a saved amount of 12.5, when it is displayed in the expense list and summary, then it is shown as 12.50.\n\n### REQ-009 Fast local response (should)\n\nPages and summaries respond quickly on the local machine, including with a large number of stored expenses.\n\n- Given 10,000 stored expenses, when the user opens the summary page, then the page is displayed within 1 second.\n- Given 10,000 stored expenses, when the user saves a new expense, then the confirmation is displayed within 1 second.\n\n### REQ-010 Clear, usable feedback (should)\n\nThe interface labels every input and shows plain-language messages for validation errors and for saved changes, so the user always knows whether an action succeeded.\n\n- Given any form in the app, when it is displayed, then every field has a visible label stating what it is.\n- Given a failed submission, when the error is shown, then the message names the field and the reason and the entered values remain in the form.\n\n## Assumptions\n\n- Single user: no accounts, login or multi-user separation; anyone with local access to the running app sees the same data.\n- The server listens on the local machine only (default port 8000) and the app is started with `python -m expensetracker`.\n- Budgets are monthly: each category has one budget amount that applies to every calendar month and is not copied or reset per month.\n- \"Getting close to the limit\" means 80% of the category budget; over budget means more than 100%.\n- Categories are a fixed list seeded at first run (Groceries, Rent, Transport, Utilities, Entertainment, Health, Other); adding custom categories is not included.\n- A single currency is used, shown without a currency selector; amounts are stored as integer cents.\n- Dates are entered as YYYY-MM-DD and default to today's date in the form.\n- The summary covers only the current calendar month; browsing past months is not included.\n- Editing and deleting saved expenses or budgets is not included in this version, since it was not requested.\n- Storage is a SQLite file in a local data directory next to the package, created automatically on first run.\n"
    },
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Design:\n[sequence] Budget overview:\n@startuml\nautonumber\ntitle View budget usage with warnings (REQ-004, REQ-005)\n\nparticipant TrackerPage\nparticipant ApiHandler\nparticipant ExpenseTrackerService\nparticipant Clock\nparticipant BudgetRepository\nparticipant ExpenseRepository\nparticipant CategoryRepository\nparticipant BudgetStatus\n\nTrackerPage -> ApiHandler : GET /api/budgets\nApiHandler -> ExpenseTrackerService : budget_overview()\nExpenseTrackerService -> Clock : current_month() = \"2026-05\"\nExpenseTrackerService -> BudgetRepository : list_all()\nBudgetRepository --> ExpenseTrackerService : [Budget(category_id=1, 10000), Budget(category_id=2, 5000)]\nExpenseTrackerService -> ExpenseRepository : sum_by_category(2026, 5)\nExpenseRepository --> ExpenseTrackerService : {1: 8500}\nExpenseTrackerService -> CategoryRepository : list_all()\nCategoryRepository --> ExpenseTrackerService : [Category(1, Groceries), Category(2, Transport)]\nExpenseTrackerService -> BudgetStatus : evaluate(\"Groceries\", 10000, 8500)\nBudgetStatus -> BudgetStatus : percent_used() = 85.0\nBudgetStatus --> ExpenseTrackerService : BudgetStatus(level=NEAR_LIMIT, spent_cents=8500)\nExpenseTrackerService -> BudgetStatus : evaluate(\"Transport\", 5000, 12000)\nBudgetStatus --> ExpenseTrackerService : BudgetStatus(level=OVER, spent_cents=12000)\nExpenseTrackerService --> ApiHandler : [BudgetStatus, BudgetStatus]\nApiHandler --> TrackerPage : 200 {budgets: [{category, budget_display, spent_display, percent, level, message}]}\nTrackerPage -> TrackerPage : renderBudgets(), showMessage(\"85% of budget used\")\n\nnote over BudgetStatus\nlevel = OK below 80%, NEAR_LIMIT from 80% up to 100%,\nOVER above 100% of the category budget (REQ-005).\nend note\n@enduml\n\n\n[component] Components:\n@startuml\ntitle Runtime parts of the local expense tracker\n\nnode \"Local machine (no external network)\" {\n  component \"Browser page\\nindex.html + app.js + style.css\" as Browser\n  component \"expensetracker server\\npython -m expensetracker\\nhttp.server.HTTPServer + JSON API\" as Server\n  database \"SQLite file\\ndata/expense_tracker.db\" as DB\n}\n\nBrowser --> Server : HTTP on 127.0.0.1:8000\\nGET /api/expenses, /api/categories, /api/budgets, /api/summary\\nPOST /api/expenses, /api/budgets\nServer --> DB : sqlite3 (Python stdlib), one connection per call\n\nnote right of Server\n  Single-threaded http.server.HTTPServer (not ThreadingHTTPServer).\n  On start-up the SQLite file and schema are created if missing, the\n  seven fixed categories are seeded, then requests are served (REQ-001, REQ-007).\nend note\n\nnote bottom of DB\n  Amounts are stored as integer cents; each repository call opens its own\n  short-lived connection, so no locking is needed (REQ-008, REQ-009).\nend note\n@enduml\n\n\n[class] Domain classes:\n@startuml\nskinparam classAttributeIconSize 0\ntitle Domain and runtime classes\n\nclass App <<entry>> {\n  {static} + main() : None\n}\n\nclass Money <<utility>> {\n  {static} + parse_amount(text : str) : int\n  {static} + format_cents(cents : int) : str\n}\n\nclass Dates <<utility>> {\n  {static} + parse_date(text : str) : date\n}\n\nclass Clock <<utility>> {\n  + today() : date\n  + current_month() : str\n}\n\nclass TrackerPage <<view>> {\n  + callApi(method : str, path : str, body : dict) : dict\n  + renderExpenses(expenses : list) : None\n  + insertRow(expense : dict) : None\n  + renderBudgets(statuses : list) : None\n  + renderSummary(summary : dict) : None\n  + showMessage(text : str, is_error : bool) : None\n}\n\nclass Expense {\n  + id : int\n  + amount_cents : int\n  + spent_on : date\n  + category_id : int\n  + amount_display() : str\n}\n\nclass Category {\n  + id : int\n  + name : str\n}\n\nclass Budget {\n  + id : int\n  + category_id : int\n  + amount_cents : int\n  + amount_display() : str\n}\n\nenum BudgetLevel {\n  OK\n  NEAR_LIMIT\n  OVER\n}\n\nclass BudgetStatus {\n  + category_name : str\n  + budget_cents : int\n  + spent_cents : int\n  + level : BudgetLevel\n  + percent_used() : float\n  + message() : str\n  {static} + evaluate(category_name : str, budget_cents : int, spent_cents : int) : BudgetStatus\n}\n\nclass MonthlySummary {\n  + month : str\n  + total_cents : int\n  + by_category : dict\n  + total_display() : str\n  + category_display(category_name : str) : str\n}\n\nclass ExpenseTrackerService {\n  - clock : Clock\n  + add_expense(amount_text : str, date_text : str, category_name : str) : Expense\n  + list_expenses() : list\n  + set_budget(category_name : str, amount_text : str) : Budget\n  + budget_overview(month : str = None) : list\n  + monthly_summary(month : str = None) : MonthlySummary\n  + list_categories() : list\n}\n\nclass ExpenseRepository {\n  + insert(expense : Expense) : int\n  + list_newest_first() : list\n  + sum_by_category(year : int, month : int) : dict\n}\n\nclass BudgetRepository {\n  + upsert(category_id : int, amount_cents : int) : Budget\n  + find_by_category(category_id : int) : Budget\n  + list_all() : list\n}\n\nclass CategoryRepository {\n  + list_all() : list\n  + find_by_name(name : str) : Category\n  + seed_defaults() : None\n}\n\nclass AppDatabase {\n  + path : str\n  + create_schema() : None\n  + connect() : Connection\n  + execute(sql : str, params : tuple) : int\n  + fetchall(sql : str, params : tuple) : list\n}\n\nclass ApiHandler {\n  + do_GET() : None\n  + do_POST() : None\n  + route_get(path : str) : tuple\n  + route_post(path : str, body : dict) : tuple\n  + send_json(status : int, payload : dict) : None\n  + send_static(path : str) : None\n}\n\nclass TrackerServer {\n  + port : int\n  + serve_forever() : None\n}\n\nclass ValidationError {\n  + field : str\n  + message : str\n}\n\nApp --> AppDatabase : creates\nApp --> ExpenseTrackerService : wires\nApp --> TrackerServer : starts\n\nTrackerPage --> ApiHandler : JSON over HTTP >\nExpenseTrackerService o-- ExpenseRepository\nExpenseTrackerService o-- BudgetRepository\nExpenseTrackerService o-- CategoryRepository\nExpenseTrackerService --> Clock : uses >\nExpenseTrackerService ..> Money\nExpenseTrackerService ..> Dates\nExpenseTrackerService ..> BudgetStatus\nExpenseTrackerService ..> MonthlySummary\nExpenseTrackerService ..> ValidationError\nExpenseRepository --> AppDatabase\nBudgetRepository --> AppDatabase\nCategoryRepository --> AppDatabase\nApiHandler --> ExpenseTrackerService\nApiHandler ..> ValidationError\nTrackerServer --> ApiHandler\nExpense --> Category : categorised by >\nBudget --> Category : limit for >\nExpense --> Money : displayed with >\nBudget --> Money : displayed with >\nBudgetStatus --> Budget : reports on >\nBudgetStatus --> Category : for >\nMonthlySummary --> Expense : totals >\n\nnote right of Money\n  parse_amount raises ValidationError(\"amount\", reason) for a missing,\n  non-numeric or non-positive amount; format_cents always prints two\n  decimals (REQ-002, REQ-008, REQ-010).\nend note\n\nnote right of Dates\n  parse_date raises ValidationError(\"date\", reason) unless the text is\n  a valid YYYY-MM-DD calendar date (REQ-002).\nend note\n\nnote bottom of AppDatabase\n  connect() opens one short-lived sqlite3 connection per call inside a\n  with block and closes it afterwards. The server is a single-threaded\n  HTTPServer, so no shared connection and no lock are needed; the file\n  is created on first run (REQ-007).\nend note\n\nnote bottom of ExpenseRepository\n  sum_by_category returns dict[int, int] keyed by category_id\n  (SELECT category_id, SUM(amount_cents) ... GROUP BY category_id);\n  the service joins the names from CategoryRepository (REQ-005, REQ-006).\nend note\n\nnote right of ExpenseTrackerService\n  month defaults to clock.current_month() when the caller passes None,\n  so a test can fix 2026-05 explicitly (REQ-005, REQ-006).\nend note\n@enduml\n\n\n[activity] Expense validation flow:\n@startuml\ntitle Validate and save an expense (REQ-002, REQ-010)\n\nstart\n:User submits amount, date, category;\n:Money.parse_amount(amount_text);\n:Dates.parse_date(date_text);\nif (amount missing, non-numeric or <= 0?) then (yes)\n  :ValidationError(\"amount\", reason);\n  :400 {field: \"amount\", message};\n  :Keep entered values in the form;\n  stop\nelse (no)\n  if (date not a valid calendar date?) then (yes)\n    :ValidationError(\"date\", reason);\n    :400 {field: \"date\", message};\n    :Keep entered values in the form;\n    stop\n  else (no)\n    if (category not in the fixed list?) then (yes)\n      :400 {field: \"category\", message};\n      :Keep entered values in the form;\n      stop\n    else (no)\n      :ExpenseRepository.insert(Expense with amount_cents);\n      :201 with the saved expense and its display strings;\n      :Insert the row at its date position and show \"Expense saved\";\n      stop\n    endif\n  endif\nendif\n@enduml\n\n\n[sequence] Log expense:\n@startuml\nautonumber\ntitle Load the list and log an expense (REQ-002, REQ-003, REQ-008, REQ-010)\n\nparticipant TrackerPage\nparticipant ApiHandler\nparticipant ExpenseTrackerService\nparticipant CategoryRepository\nparticipant ExpenseRepository\n\n== page load (REQ-003) ==\nTrackerPage -> ApiHandler : GET /api/expenses\nApiHandler -> ExpenseTrackerService : list_expenses()\nExpenseTrackerService -> ExpenseRepository : list_newest_first()\nExpenseRepository --> ExpenseTrackerService : [Expense(id=6), ...]\nExpenseTrackerService --> ApiHandler : list\nApiHandler --> TrackerPage : 200 {expenses: [...]}\nTrackerPage -> TrackerPage : renderExpenses()\n\n== submit the form (REQ-002) ==\nTrackerPage -> ApiHandler : POST /api/expenses {amount: \"12.50\", date: \"2026-05-03\", category: \"Groceries\"}\nApiHandler -> ExpenseTrackerService : add_expense(\"12.50\", \"2026-05-03\", \"Groceries\")\nExpenseTrackerService -> ExpenseTrackerService : Money.parse_amount(\"12.50\") = 1250\nExpenseTrackerService -> ExpenseTrackerService : Dates.parse_date(\"2026-05-03\")\nExpenseTrackerService -> CategoryRepository : find_by_name(\"Groceries\")\nCategoryRepository --> ExpenseTrackerService : Category(id=1, name=Groceries)\nExpenseTrackerService -> ExpenseRepository : insert(Expense(amount_cents=1250, spent_on=2026-05-03, category_id=1))\nExpenseRepository --> ExpenseTrackerService : 7\nExpenseTrackerService --> ApiHandler : Expense(id=7)\nApiHandler --> TrackerPage : 201 {id: 7, amount_display: \"12.50\", date: \"2026-05-03\", category: \"Groceries\"}\nTrackerPage -> TrackerPage : insertRow(...), showMessage(\"Expense saved\")\n\nnote over ApiHandler\nInvalid amount or date: Money.parse_amount / Dates.parse_date raise a\nValidationError, answered with 400 {field, message}. Nothing is inserted, the\npage keeps the entered values and the list is not refetched (REQ-002, REQ-010).\nend note\n@enduml\n\n\n[sequence] Monthly summary:\n@startuml\nautonumber\ntitle Monthly spending summary (REQ-006, REQ-008, REQ-009)\n\nparticipant TrackerPage\nparticipant ApiHandler\nparticipant ExpenseTrackerService\nparticipant Clock\nparticipant ExpenseRepository\nparticipant CategoryRepository\nparticipant MonthlySummary\n\nTrackerPage -> ApiHandler : GET /api/summary\nApiHandler -> ExpenseTrackerService : monthly_summary()\nExpenseTrackerService -> Clock : current_month() = \"2026-05\"\nExpenseTrackerService -> ExpenseRepository : sum_by_category(2026, 5)\nExpenseRepository --> ExpenseTrackerService : {1: 4000, 2: 6000}\nExpenseTrackerService -> CategoryRepository : list_all()\nCategoryRepository --> ExpenseTrackerService : [Category(1, Groceries), Category(2, Transport)]\nExpenseTrackerService -> MonthlySummary : by_category = {Groceries: 4000, Transport: 6000}, total_cents = 10000\nMonthlySummary --> ExpenseTrackerService : summary\nExpenseTrackerService -> MonthlySummary : total_display()\nMonthlySummary --> ExpenseTrackerService : \"100.00\"\nExpenseTrackerService -> MonthlySummary : category_display(\"Groceries\")\nMonthlySummary --> ExpenseTrackerService : \"40.00\"\nExpenseTrackerService --> ApiHandler : MonthlySummary(month=\"2026-05\")\nApiHandler --> TrackerPage : 200 {month, total_display: \"100.00\", categories: [{name, total_display}]}\nTrackerPage -> TrackerPage : renderSummary()\n\nnote over ExpenseRepository\nSUM(amount_cents) GROUP BY category_id, filtered by spent_on between the\nfirst and last day of the month; rows from other months are excluded by the\nquery. The service maps category_id to names (REQ-006, REQ-009).\nend note\n@enduml\n\n\n[sequence] Set budget:\n@startuml\nautonumber\ntitle Set or update a monthly budget (REQ-004)\n\nparticipant TrackerPage\nparticipant ApiHandler\nparticipant ExpenseTrackerService\nparticipant CategoryRepository\nparticipant BudgetRepository\n\nTrackerPage -> ApiHandler : POST /api/budgets {category: \"Groceries\", amount: \"350.00\"}\nApiHandler -> ExpenseTrackerService : set_budget(\"Groceries\", \"350.00\")\nExpenseTrackerService -> ExpenseTrackerService : Money.parse_amount(\"350.00\") = 35000\nExpenseTrackerService -> CategoryRepository : find_by_name(\"Groceries\")\nCategoryRepository --> ExpenseTrackerService : Category(id=1)\nExpenseTrackerService -> BudgetRepository : upsert(1, 35000)\nBudgetRepository --> ExpenseTrackerService : Budget(id=3, category_id=1, amount_cents=35000)\nExpenseTrackerService --> ApiHandler : Budget\nApiHandler --> TrackerPage : 200 {category: \"Groceries\", budget_display: \"350.00\"}\nTrackerPage -> TrackerPage : showMessage(\"Budget saved\"), update Groceries row\n\nnote over ApiHandler\nNegative, missing or non-numeric amount: Money.parse_amount raises\nValidationError, answered with 400 {field: \"amount\", message}; no budget\nrow is written (REQ-004, REQ-010).\nend note\n@enduml\n\n\n[sequence] Startup and storage:\n@startuml\nautonumber\ntitle Start-up, schema creation and recovery of stored data (REQ-001, REQ-007)\n\nparticipant App\nparticipant AppDatabase\nparticipant CategoryRepository\nparticipant ExpenseRepository\nparticipant BudgetRepository\nparticipant ExpenseTrackerService\nparticipant TrackerServer\n\nnote over App\npython -m expensetracker runs App.main(), which wires the parts below\nin this order and then serves the tracker page (REQ-001).\nend note\nApp -> AppDatabase : new AppDatabase(\"data/expense_tracker.db\")\nApp -> AppDatabase : create_schema()\nnote right of AppDatabase\n  sqlite3.connect() creates data/expense_tracker.db when the file is\n  missing, then CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS categories, expenses, budgets.\nend note\nAppDatabase --> App : schema ready\nApp -> CategoryRepository : new CategoryRepository(db)\nApp -> CategoryRepository : seed_defaults()\nnote right of CategoryRepository\n  Seeds Groceries, Rent, Transport, Utilities, Entertainment, Health and\n  Other only when the table is empty, so a restart keeps existing rows.\nend note\nApp -> ExpenseRepository : new ExpenseRepository(db)\nApp -> BudgetRepository : new BudgetRepository(db)\nApp -> ExpenseTrackerService : new ExpenseTrackerService(expenses, budgets, categories, Clock())\nApp -> TrackerServer : new TrackerServer(port=8000, handler=ApiHandler(service))\nApp -> TrackerServer : serve_forever()\nTrackerServer --> App : serving on 127.0.0.1:8000\n\nnote over TrackerServer\nSingle-threaded HTTPServer; every repository call opens its own short-lived\nsqlite3 connection, so expenses and budgets are simply re-read from the file\nafter a restart (REQ-007).\nend note\n@enduml\n\n\n[use_case] Use cases:\n@startuml\nleft to right direction\nskinparam packageStyle rectangle\n\nactor \"Local user\" as User\n\nrectangle \"Expense Tracker (local web app)\" {\n  usecase \"Start the tracker server\" as UC1\n  usecase \"Log an expense\" as UC2\n  usecase \"View recorded expenses\" as UC3\n  usecase \"Set a monthly category budget\" as UC4\n  usecase \"View budget usage and warnings\" as UC5\n  usecase \"View monthly spending summary\" as UC6\n}\n\nUser --> UC1\nUser --> UC2\nUser --> UC3\nUser --> UC4\nUser --> UC5\nUser --> UC6\n\nUC2 ..> UC3 : <<include>>\nUC5 ..> UC6 : <<include>>\nUC5 ..> UC4 : <<extend>>\n@enduml\n"
    },
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Code under test:\n### expensetracker/api.py\n\"\"\"ApiHandler: the JSON API and the static file server of the tracker page.\n\nImplements the ApiHandler class of the domain class diagram and the routing\nshown in the \"Log expense\", \"Set budget\", \"Budget overview\" and \"Monthly\nsummary\" sequence diagrams.\nTrace: REQ-001, REQ-002, REQ-003, REQ-004, REQ-005, REQ-006, REQ-010\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport json\nfrom http.server import BaseHTTPRequestHandler\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom typing import ClassVar\nfrom urllib.parse import urlsplit\n\nfrom .errors import ValidationError\nfrom .models import BudgetStatus\nfrom .money import Money\nfrom .service import ExpenseTrackerService\n\nSTATIC_DIR = Path(__file__).resolve().parent / \"static\"\n\nCONTENT_TYPES: dict[str, str] = {\n    \".html\": \"text/html; charset=utf-8\",\n    \".css\": \"text/css; charset=utf-8\",\n    \".js\": \"text/javascript; charset=utf-8\",\n    \".json\": \"application/json; charset=utf-8\",\n    \".svg\": \"image/svg+xml\",\n    \".ico\": \"image/x-icon\",\n}\n\n\nclass ApiHandler(BaseHTTPRequestHandler):\n    \"\"\"Serves /api/* as JSON and everything else from the static directory.\n\n    ``ApiHandler(service)`` returns a subclass with the service bound, so the\n    server can be built exactly as the start-up sequence shows:\n    ``TrackerServer(port=8000, handler=ApiHandler(service))``.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    service: ClassVar[ExpenseTrackerService]\n    static_dir: ClassVar[Path] = STATIC_DIR\n\n    def __new__(cls, *args, **kwargs):\n        if len(args) == 1 and not kwargs and isinstance(args[0], ExpenseTrackerService):\n            return type(f\"{cls.__name__}Bound\", (cls,), {\"service\": args[0]})\n        return super().__new__(cls)\n\n    # -- HTTP verbs ---------------------------------------------------------\n\n    def do_GET(self) -> None:\n        path = urlsplit(self.path).path\n        if not path.startswith(\"/api/\"):\n            self.send_static(path)\n            return\n        try:\n            status, payload = self.route_get(path)\n        except ValidationError as error:\n            status, payload = 400, {\"field\": error.field, \"message\": error.message}\n        except Exception:  # noqa: BLE001 - never leak a traceback to the page\n            status, payload = 500, {\"error\": \"Internal server error\"}\n        self.send_json(status, payload)\n\n    def do_POST(self) -> None:\n        path = urlsplit(self.path).path\n        length = int(self.headers.get(\"Content-Length\") or 0)\n        raw = self.rfile.read(length) if length > 0 else b\"\"\n        try:\n            body = json.loads(raw.decode(\"utf-8\") or \"{}\")\n        except (UnicodeDecodeError, json.JSONDecodeError):\n            self.send_json(400, {\"field\": \"body\", \"message\": \"Request body must be valid JSON.\"})\n            return\n        if not isinstance(body, dict):\n            self.send_json(400, {\"field\": \"body\", \"message\": \"Request body must be a JSON object.\"})\n            return\n        try:\n            status, payload = self.route_post(path, body)\n        except ValidationError as error:\n            status, payload = 400, {\"field\": error.field, \"message\": error.message}\n        except Exception:  # noqa: BLE001\n            status, payload = 500, {\"error\": \"Internal server error\"}\n        self.send_json(status, payload)\n\n    # -- routing ------------------------------------------------------------\n\n    def route_get(self, path: str) -> tuple[int, dict]:\n        \"\"\"Dispatch a GET request: expenses, categories, budgets or summary.\"\"\"\n        service = self.service\n        names = {category.id: category.name for category in service.list_categories()}\n        if path == \"/api/expenses\":\n            return 200, {\n                \"expenses\": [\n                    {\n                        \"id\": expense.id,\n                        \"amount_display\": expense.amount_display(),\n                        \"date\": expense.spent_on.isoformat(),\n                        \"category\": names.get(expense.category_id, \"Unknown\"),\n                    }\n                    for expense in service.list_expenses()\n                ]\n            }\n        if path == \"/api/categories\":\n            return 200, {\n                \"categories\": [\n                    {\"id\": category.id, \"name\": category.name}\n                    for category in service.list_categories()\n                ]\n            }\n        if path == \"/api/budgets\":\n            return 200, {\"budgets\": [self._budget_payload(item) for item in service.budget_overview()]}\n        if path == \"/api/summary\":\n            summary = service.monthly_summary()\n            return 200, {\n                \"month\": summary.month,\n                \"total_display\": summary.total_display(),\n                \"categories\": [\n                    {\"name\": name, \"total_display\": summary.category_display(name)}\n                    for name in summary.by_category\n                ],\n            }\n        return 404, {\"error\": \"Not found\"}\n\n    def route_post(self, path: str, body: dict) -> tuple[int, dict]:\n        \"\"\"Dispatch a POST request: save an expense or set a budget.\"\"\"\n        service = self.service\n        if path == \"/api/expenses\":\n            expense = service.add_expense(body.get(\"amount\"), body.get(\"date\"), body.get(\"category\"))\n            names = {category.id: category.name for category in service.list_categories()}\n            return 201, {\n                \"id\": expense.id,\n                \"amount_display\": expense.amount_display(),\n                \"date\": expense.spent_on.isoformat(),\n                \"category\": names.get(expense.category_id, \"Unknown\"),\n            }\n        if path == \"/api/budgets\":\n            budget = service.set_budget(body.get(\"category\"), body.get(\"amount\"))\n            names = {category.id: category.name for category in service.list_categories()}\n            return 200, {\n                \"category\": names.get(budget.category_id, \"Unknown\"),\n                \"budget_display\": budget.amount_display(),\n            }\n        return 404, {\"error\": \"Not found\"}\n\n    # -- responses ----------------------------------------------------------\n\n    def send_json(self, status: int, payload: dict) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Write a JSON response with the given HTTP status.\"\"\"\n        data = json.dumps(payload).encode(\"utf-8\")\n        self.send_response(status)\n        self.send_header(\"Content-Type\", \"application/json; charset=utf-8\")\n        self.send_header(\"Content-Length\", str(len(data)))\n        self.send_header(\"Cache-Control\", \"no-store\")\n        self.end_headers()\n        self.wfile.write(data)\n\n    def send_static(self, path: str) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Serve index.html, app.js and style.css from the static directory.\"\"\"\n        name = path.lstrip(\"/\") or \"index.html\"\n        if name.endswith(\"/\"):\n            name += \"index.html\"\n        root = self.static_dir.resolve()\n        target = (root / name).resolve()\n        try:\n            target.relative_to(root)\n        except ValueError:\n            self.send_json(404, {\"error\": \"Not found\"})\n            return\n        if not target.is_file():\n            self.send_json(404, {\"error\": \"Not found\"})\n            return\n        data = target.read_bytes()\n        self.send_response(200)\n        self.send_header(\n            \"Content-Type\", CONTENT_TYPES.get(target.suffix, \"application/octet-stream\")\n        )\n        self.send_header(\"Content-Length\", str(len(data)))\n        self.send_header(\"Cache-Control\", \"no-store\")\n        self.end_headers()\n        self.wfile.write(data)\n\n    # -- helpers ------------------------------------------------------------\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def _budget_payload(status: BudgetStatus) -> dict:\n        \"\"\"Shape one BudgetStatus for the budget overview response.\"\"\"\n        return {\n            \"category\": status.category_name,\n            \"budget_display\": Money.format_cents(status.budget_cents),\n            \"spent_display\": Money.format_cents(status.spent_cents),\n            \"percent\": status.percent_used(),\n            \"level\": status.level.value,\n            \"message\": status.message(),\n        }\n\n\n### expensetracker/app.py\n\"\"\"App: the entry point that wires storage, service and server together.\n\nImplements the App class of the domain class diagram and the \"Startup and\nstorage\" sequence diagram.\nTrace: REQ-001, REQ-007\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport argparse\nimport threading\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom urllib.request import urlopen\n\nfrom .api import ApiHandler\nfrom .clock import Clock\nfrom .database import AppDatabase\nfrom .page import TrackerPage\nfrom .repositories import BudgetRepository, CategoryRepository, ExpenseRepository\nfrom .server import TrackerServer\nfrom .service import ExpenseTrackerService\n\nDEFAULT_PORT = 8000\nDATA_FILE = Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent / \"data\" / \"expense_tracker.db\"\n\n\nclass App:\n    \"\"\"Builds the object graph in the order the start-up sequence shows.\"\"\"\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def main(argv: list[str] | None = None) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Create the schema, seed categories, wire the service and serve.\"\"\"\n        parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(\n            prog=\"python -m expensetracker\",\n            description=\"Local single-user expense tracker.\",\n        )\n        parser.add_argument(\"--port\", type=int, default=DEFAULT_PORT, help=\"port to listen on\")\n        parser.add_argument(\n            \"--check\",\n            action=\"store_true\",\n            help=\"start on a free port, request the main page once, print the status and exit\",\n        )\n        args = parser.parse_args(argv)\n\n        database = AppDatabase(str(DATA_FILE))\n        database.create_schema()\n\n        categories = CategoryRepository(database)\n        categories.seed_defaults()\n        expenses = ExpenseRepository(database)\n        budgets = BudgetRepository(database)\n        service = ExpenseTrackerService(expenses, budgets, categories, Clock())\n\n        server = TrackerServer(port=0 if args.check else args.port, handler=ApiHandler(service))\n\n        if args.check:\n            App._smoke_test(server)\n            return\n\n        print(f\"Expense tracker running at http://127.0.0.1:{args.port}/ (Ctrl+C to stop)\")\n        try:\n            server.serve_forever()\n        except KeyboardInterrupt:\n            print(\"\\nStopped.\")\n        finally:\n            server._shutdown()\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def _smoke_test(server: TrackerServer) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Start the server, request the main page once, print its status, exit.\"\"\"\n        thread = threading.Thread(target=server.serve_forever, daemon=True)\n        thread.start()\n        base_url = f\"http://127.0.0.1:{server._bound_port()}\"\n        try:\n            with urlopen(f\"{base_url}/\", timeout=10) as response:\n                print(f\"GET / -> {response.status}\")\n            page = TrackerPage(base_url)\n            page.renderExpenses(page.callApi(\"GET\", \"/api/expenses\").get(\"expenses\", []))\n            page.renderBudgets(page.callApi(\"GET\", \"/api/budgets\").get(\"budgets\", []))\n            summary = page.callApi(\"GET\", \"/api/summary\")\n            page.renderSummary(summary)\n            print(\n                f\"GET /api/summary -> month {summary.get('month')} \"\n                f\"total {summary.get('total_display')}\"\n            )\n        finally:\n            server._shutdown()\n            thread.join(timeout=5)\n\n\n### expensetracker/clock.py\n\"\"\"Clock: the source of \"today\" and of the current calendar month.\n\nImplements the Clock utility class of the domain class diagram.\nTrace: REQ-005, REQ-006\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nfrom datetime import date\n\n\nclass Clock:\n    \"\"\"Wall-clock helper; tests can subclass it to fix the current month.\"\"\"\n\n    def today(self) -> date:\n        \"\"\"The current local date.\"\"\"\n        return date.today()\n\n    def current_month(self) -> str:\n        \"\"\"The current calendar month as YYYY-MM, e.g. \"2026-05\".\"\"\"\n        return self.today().strftime(\"%Y-%m\")\n\n\n### expensetracker/database.py\n\"\"\"AppDatabase: SQLite file storage, schema creation and short-lived connections.\n\nImplements the AppDatabase class of the domain class diagram.\nTrace: REQ-001, REQ-007, REQ-009\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport sqlite3\nfrom contextlib import closing\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nSCHEMA = \"\"\"\nCREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS categories (\n    id   INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT,\n    name TEXT NOT NULL UNIQUE\n);\n\nCREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS expenses (\n    id           INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT,\n    amount_cents INTEGER NOT NULL,\n    spent_on     TEXT NOT NULL,\n    category_id  INTEGER NOT NULL REFERENCES categories(id)\n);\n\nCREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_expenses_spent_on ON expenses(spent_on);\n\nCREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS budgets (\n    id           INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT,\n    category_id  INTEGER NOT NULL UNIQUE REFERENCES categories(id),\n    amount_cents INTEGER NOT NULL\n);\n\"\"\"\n\n\nclass AppDatabase:\n    \"\"\"Owns the SQLite file path and opens one short-lived connection per call.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, path: str) -> None:\n        self.path = path\n\n    def connect(self) -> sqlite3.Connection:\n        \"\"\"Open a new connection, creating the data directory when missing.\"\"\"\n        parent = Path(self.path).parent\n        if str(parent) and not parent.exists():\n            parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n        connection = sqlite3.connect(self.path)\n        connection.row_factory = sqlite3.Row\n        return connection\n\n    def create_schema(self) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Create the tables when the file is new; keep existing data untouched.\"\"\"\n        with closing(self.connect()) as connection:\n            connection.executescript(SCHEMA)\n            connection.commit()\n\n    def execute(self, sql: str, params: tuple = ()) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Run a writing statement and return the new row id (0 when none).\"\"\"\n        with closing(self.connect()) as connection:\n            cursor = connection.execute(sql, params)\n            connection.commit()\n            return int(cursor.lastrowid or 0)\n\n    def fetchall(self, sql: str, params: tuple = ()) -> list[sqlite3.Row]:\n        \"\"\"Run a reading statement and return all rows.\"\"\"\n        with closing(self.connect()) as connection:\n            cursor = connection.execute(sql, params)\n            return list(cursor.fetchall())\n\n\n### expensetracker/dates.py\n\"\"\"Dates: strict YYYY-MM-DD parsing for expense dates.\n\nImplements the Dates utility class of the domain class diagram.\nTrace: REQ-002, REQ-010\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport re\nfrom datetime import date\n\nfrom .errors import ValidationError\n\n_ISO_DATE = re.compile(r\"\\d{4}-\\d{2}-\\d{2}\")\n\n\nclass Dates:\n    \"\"\"Parses the date text typed by the user into a real calendar date.\"\"\"\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def parse_date(text: str) -> date:\n        \"\"\"Return the date, or raise ValidationError(\"date\", ...).\"\"\"\n        if text is None:\n            raise ValidationError(\"date\", \"Date is required.\")\n        raw = str(text).strip()\n        if not raw:\n            raise ValidationError(\"date\", \"Date is required.\")\n        if not _ISO_DATE.fullmatch(raw):\n            raise ValidationError(\"date\", \"Date must be a valid date in YYYY-MM-DD format.\")\n        try:\n            return date.fromisoformat(raw)\n        except ValueError:\n            raise ValidationError(\"date\", \"Date must be a valid date in YYYY-MM-DD format.\") from None\n\n\n### expensetracker/errors.py\n\"\"\"ValidationError: the single error type used for user input problems.\n\nImplements the ValidationError class of the domain class diagram.\nTrace: REQ-002, REQ-004, REQ-010\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\n\nclass ValidationError(Exception):\n    \"\"\"A rejected user input, naming the field and the plain-language reason.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, field: str, message: str) -> None:\n        super().__init__(message)\n        self.field = field\n        self.message = message\n\n\n### expensetracker/__init__.py\n\"\"\"expensetracker: a local, single-user expense tracker served by Python.\n\nPackage root for the classes of the approved design.\nTrace: REQ-001\n\"\"\"\n\n__all__ = [\n    \"app\",\n    \"api\",\n    \"clock\",\n    \"database\",\n    \"dates\",\n    \"errors\",\n    \"models\",\n    \"money\",\n    \"page\",\n    \"repositories\",\n    \"server\",\n    \"service\",\n]\n\n\n### expensetracker/__main__.py\n\"\"\"Module entry point: ``python -m expensetracker`` starts the tracker server.\n\nImplements the <<entry>> role of App in the domain class diagram.\nTrace: REQ-001\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom .app import App\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    App.main()\n\n\n### expensetracker/models.py\n\"\"\"Domain models: Expense, Category, Budget, BudgetLevel, BudgetStatus, MonthlySummary.\n\nImplements the model classes of the domain class diagram.\nTrace: REQ-003, REQ-004, REQ-005, REQ-006, REQ-008\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass, field\nfrom datetime import date\nfrom enum import Enum\n\nfrom .money import Money\n\n\n@dataclass\nclass Category:\n    \"\"\"A fixed spending category such as Groceries.\"\"\"\n\n    id: int\n    name: str\n\n\n@dataclass\nclass Expense:\n    \"\"\"One recorded expense; the amount is stored as integer cents.\"\"\"\n\n    id: int\n    amount_cents: int\n    spent_on: date\n    category_id: int\n\n    def amount_display(self) -> str:\n        \"\"\"The amount with exactly two decimals, e.g. \"12.50\".\"\"\"\n        return Money.format_cents(self.amount_cents)\n\n\n@dataclass\nclass Budget:\n    \"\"\"The monthly limit of one category, in integer cents.\"\"\"\n\n    id: int\n    category_id: int\n    amount_cents: int\n\n    def amount_display(self) -> str:\n        \"\"\"The budget with exactly two decimals, e.g. \"300.00\".\"\"\"\n        return Money.format_cents(self.amount_cents)\n\n\nclass BudgetLevel(Enum):\n    \"\"\"How far this month's spending has gone against a budget.\"\"\"\n\n    OK = \"OK\"\n    NEAR_LIMIT = \"NEAR_LIMIT\"\n    OVER = \"OVER\"\n\n\n@dataclass\nclass BudgetStatus:\n    \"\"\"Budget usage of one category for one month, with its warning level.\"\"\"\n\n    category_name: str\n    budget_cents: int\n    spent_cents: int\n    level: BudgetLevel\n\n    def percent_used(self) -> float:\n        \"\"\"Share of the budget used this month, in percent, one decimal.\"\"\"\n        if self.budget_cents <= 0:\n            return 0.0\n        return round(self.spent_cents * 100.0 / self.budget_cents, 1)\n\n    def message(self) -> str:\n        \"\"\"A plain-language usage message, e.g. \"Close to the limit: 85% of budget used\".\"\"\"\n        percent = self.percent_used()\n        text = f\"{percent:.0f}\" if float(percent).is_integer() else f\"{percent:.1f}\"\n        if self.level is BudgetLevel.OVER:\n            return f\"Over budget: {text}% used\"\n        if self.level is BudgetLevel.NEAR_LIMIT:\n            return f\"Close to the limit: {text}% of budget used\"\n        return f\"{text}% of budget used\"\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def evaluate(category_name: str, budget_cents: int, spent_cents: int) -> \"BudgetStatus\":\n        \"\"\"Classify spending: OK below 80%, NEAR_LIMIT 80-100%, OVER above 100%.\"\"\"\n        if budget_cents <= 0:\n            level = BudgetLevel.OK\n        else:\n            percent = spent_cents * 100.0 / budget_cents\n            if percent > 100.0:\n                level = BudgetLevel.OVER\n            elif percent >= 80.0:\n                level = BudgetLevel.NEAR_LIMIT\n            else:\n                level = BudgetLevel.OK\n        return BudgetStatus(\n            category_name=category_name,\n            budget_cents=budget_cents,\n            spent_cents=spent_cents,\n            level=level,\n        )\n\n\n@dataclass\nclass MonthlySummary:\n    \"\"\"Total spending of one calendar month, overall and per category.\"\"\"\n\n    month: str\n    total_cents: int\n    by_category: dict = field(default_factory=dict)\n\n    def total_display(self) -> str:\n        \"\"\"The month total with exactly two decimals, e.g. \"100.00\".\"\"\"\n        return Money.format_cents(self.total_cents)\n\n    def category_display(self, category_name: str) -> str:\n        \"\"\"The month total of one category, e.g. \"40.00\"; \"0.00\" when absent.\"\"\"\n        return Money.format_cents(int(self.by_category.get(category_name, 0)))\n\n\n### expensetracker/money.py\n\"\"\"Money: exact parsing and formatting of monetary amounts in integer cents.\n\nImplements the Money utility class of the domain class diagram.\nTrace: REQ-002, REQ-004, REQ-008, REQ-010\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nfrom decimal import ROUND_HALF_UP, Decimal, InvalidOperation\n\nfrom .errors import ValidationError\n\n\nclass Money:\n    \"\"\"Converts between user text and integer cents without float drift.\"\"\"\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def parse_amount(text: str) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Return the amount in cents, or raise ValidationError(\"amount\", ...).\"\"\"\n        if text is None:\n            raise ValidationError(\"amount\", \"Amount is required.\")\n        raw = str(text).strip()\n        if not raw:\n            raise ValidationError(\"amount\", \"Amount is required.\")\n        try:\n            value = Decimal(raw)\n        except (InvalidOperation, ValueError):\n            raise ValidationError(\"amount\", \"Amount must be a number, for example 12.50.\") from None\n        if not value.is_finite():\n            raise ValidationError(\"amount\", \"Amount must be a number, for example 12.50.\")\n        if value <= 0:\n            raise ValidationError(\"amount\", \"Amount must be greater than zero.\")\n        cents = (value * 100).to_integral_value(rounding=ROUND_HALF_UP)\n        return int(cents)\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def format_cents(cents: int) -> str:\n        \"\"\"Format integer cents with exactly two decimals, e.g. 1250 -> \"12.50\".\"\"\"\n        value = int(cents)\n        sign = \"-\" if value < 0 else \"\"\n        value = abs(value)\n        return f\"{sign}{value // 100}.{value % 100:02d}\"\n\n\n### expensetracker/page.py\n\"\"\"TrackerPage: the tracker page view, usable without a browser.\n\nImplements the TrackerPage class of the domain class diagram. The browser runs\nthe same view in ``static/app.js`` against the same JSON API; this Python twin\nrenders the expense list, the budget table, the monthly summary and the status\nmessage into markup strings, so the page's operations exist as Python and are\nexercised by ``python -m expensetracker --check``.\nTrace: REQ-002, REQ-003, REQ-004, REQ-005, REQ-006, REQ-010\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport html\nimport json\nfrom urllib.error import HTTPError\nfrom urllib.request import Request, urlopen\n\nDEFAULT_BASE_URL = \"http://127.0.0.1:8000\"\n\n\nclass TrackerPage:\n    \"\"\"The page as a view object: JSON calls in, rendered parts out.\n\n    The rendered markup is kept in private fields so a caller (or a test) can\n    inspect what the page would show, without needing a browser.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, base_url: str = DEFAULT_BASE_URL) -> None:\n        self._base_url = (base_url or DEFAULT_BASE_URL).rstrip(\"/\")\n        self._expense_rows: list[tuple[str, int, str]] = []\n        self._budget_rows: list[str] = []\n        self._summary_html = \"\"\n        self._message_html = \"\"\n\n    # -- API access ---------------------------------------------------------\n\n    def callApi(self, method: str, path: str, body: dict | None = None) -> dict:\n        \"\"\"Call the local JSON API and return the decoded payload.\"\"\"\n        data = None\n        headers: dict[str, str] = {}\n        if body is not None:\n            data = json.dumps(body).encode(\"utf-8\")\n            headers[\"Content-Type\"] = \"application/json\"\n        request = Request(self._base_url + path, data=data, headers=headers, method=method)\n        try:\n            with urlopen(request, timeout=10) as response:\n                return json.loads(response.read().decode(\"utf-8\") or \"{}\")\n        except HTTPError as error:\n            return json.loads(error.read().decode(\"utf-8\") or \"{}\")\n\n    # -- rendering ----------------------------------------------------------\n\n    def renderExpenses(self, expenses: list) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Replace the expense list with the given expenses (newest first).\"\"\"\n        self._expense_rows = [\n            (\n                str(expense.get(\"date\", \"\")),\n                int(expense.get(\"id\") or 0),\n                self._build_row(expense),\n            )\n            for expense in expenses or []\n        ]\n\n    def insertRow(self, expense: dict) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Insert one saved expense at its date position without refetching.\"\"\"\n        entry = (\n            str(expense.get(\"date\", \"\")),\n            int(expense.get(\"id\") or 0),\n            self._build_row(expense),\n        )\n        for index, existing in enumerate(self._expense_rows):\n            if existing[0] < entry[0] or (existing[0] == entry[0] and existing[1] < entry[1]):\n                self._expense_rows.insert(index, entry)\n                return\n        self._expense_rows.append(entry)\n\n    def renderBudgets(self, statuses: list) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Render each budgeted category with its usage and warning state.\"\"\"\n        self._budget_rows = [self._build_budget_row(status) for status in statuses or []]\n\n    def renderSummary(self, summary: dict) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Render the current month total and its per-category breakdown.\"\"\"\n        month = html.escape(str(summary.get(\"month\", \"\")))\n        total = html.escape(str(summary.get(\"total_display\", \"0.00\")))\n        categories = summary.get(\"categories\") or []\n        if categories:\n            items = \"\".join(\n                \"<li><span>\"\n                + html.escape(str(category.get(\"name\", \"\")))\n                + '</span><span class=\"amount\">'\n                + html.escape(str(category.get(\"total_display\", \"0.00\")))\n                + \"</span></li>\"\n                for category in categories\n            )\n        else:\n            items = '<li class=\"empty\">No spending recorded this month yet.</li>'\n        self._summary_html = (\n            '<p class=\"summary-total\">Total spent <span class=\"muted\">'\n            + month\n            + '</span>: <strong>'\n            + total\n            + '</strong></p><ul class=\"summary-list\">'\n            + items\n            + \"</ul>\"\n        )\n\n    def showMessage(self, text: str, is_error: bool) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Show a plain-language confirmation or validation message.\"\"\"\n        if not text:\n            self._message_html = \"\"\n            return\n        css_class = \"message error\" if is_error else \"message success\"\n        role = \"alert\" if is_error else \"status\"\n        self._message_html = (\n            f'<p class=\"{css_class}\" role=\"{role}\">{html.escape(str(text))}</p>'\n        )\n\n    # -- helpers ------------------------------------------------------------\n\n    def _build_row(self, expense: dict) -> str:\n        \"\"\"One table row for an expense: date, category and amount.\"\"\"\n        date_cell = html.escape(str(expense.get(\"date\", \"\")))\n        category_cell = html.escape(str(expense.get(\"category\", \"\")))\n        amount_cell = html.escape(str(expense.get(\"amount_display\", \"0.00\")))\n        return (\n            f\"<tr><td>{date_cell}</td><td>{category_cell}</td>\"\n            f'<td class=\"amount\">{amount_cell}</td></tr>'\n        )\n\n    def _build_budget_row(self, status: dict) -> str:\n        \"\"\"One table row for a budget: category, budget, spent and status text.\"\"\"\n        level = str(status.get(\"level\", \"OK\")).lower()\n        message = html.escape(str(status.get(\"message\", \"\")))\n        badge = \"\"\n        if level != \"ok\":\n            label = \"Over budget\" if level == \"over\" else \"Close to limit\"\n            badge = f'<span class=\"badge\">{label}</span>'\n        category_cell = html.escape(str(status.get(\"category\", \"\")))\n        budget_cell = html.escape(str(status.get(\"budget_display\", \"0.00\")))\n        spent_cell = html.escape(str(status.get(\"spent_display\", \"0.00\")))\n        return (\n            f'<tr class=\"level-{level}\"><td>{category_cell}</td>'\n            f'<td class=\"amount\">{budget_cell}</td>'\n            f'<td class=\"amount\">{spent_cell}</td>'\n            f'<td class=\"budget-message\">{badge}{message}</td></tr>'\n        )\n\n\n### expensetracker/repositories.py\n\"\"\"SQLite repositories: ExpenseRepository, BudgetRepository, CategoryRepository.\n\nImplements the three repository classes of the domain class diagram.\nTrace: REQ-003, REQ-004, REQ-005, REQ-006, REQ-007, REQ-009\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nfrom datetime import date\n\nfrom .database import AppDatabase\nfrom .models import Budget, Category, Expense\n\nDEFAULT_CATEGORIES: tuple[str, ...] = (\n    \"Groceries\",\n    \"Rent\",\n    \"Transport\",\n    \"Utilities\",\n    \"Entertainment\",\n    \"Health\",\n    \"Other\",\n)\n\n\nclass ExpenseRepository:\n    \"\"\"Reads and writes the expenses table.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, db: AppDatabase) -> None:\n        self._db = db\n\n    def insert(self, expense: Expense) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Store one expense and return its new id.\"\"\"\n        return self._db.execute(\n            \"INSERT INTO expenses (amount_cents, spent_on, category_id) VALUES (?, ?, ?)\",\n            (expense.amount_cents, expense.spent_on.isoformat(), expense.category_id),\n        )\n\n    def list_newest_first(self) -> list[Expense]:\n        \"\"\"All expenses ordered by date from newest to oldest.\"\"\"\n        rows = self._db.fetchall(\n            \"SELECT id, amount_cents, spent_on, category_id FROM expenses \"\n            \"ORDER BY spent_on DESC, id DESC\"\n        )\n        return [\n            Expense(\n                id=int(row[\"id\"]),\n                amount_cents=int(row[\"amount_cents\"]),\n                spent_on=date.fromisoformat(str(row[\"spent_on\"])),\n                category_id=int(row[\"category_id\"]),\n            )\n            for row in rows\n        ]\n\n    def sum_by_category(self, year: int, month: int) -> dict[int, int]:\n        \"\"\"Spent cents per category_id for the given calendar month.\"\"\"\n        start = date(year, month, 1)\n        end = date(year + 1, 1, 1) if month == 12 else date(year, month + 1, 1)\n        rows = self._db.fetchall(\n            \"SELECT category_id, SUM(amount_cents) AS total FROM expenses \"\n            \"WHERE spent_on >= ? AND spent_on < ? GROUP BY category_id\",\n            (start.isoformat(), end.isoformat()),\n        )\n        return {int(row[\"category_id\"]): int(row[\"total\"]) for row in rows}\n\n\nclass BudgetRepository:\n    \"\"\"Reads and writes the one-budget-per-category table.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, db: AppDatabase) -> None:\n        self._db = db\n\n    def upsert(self, category_id: int, amount_cents: int) -> Budget:\n        \"\"\"Insert the budget of a category or replace its amount.\"\"\"\n        existing = self.find_by_category(category_id)\n        if existing is None:\n            new_id = self._db.execute(\n                \"INSERT INTO budgets (category_id, amount_cents) VALUES (?, ?)\",\n                (category_id, amount_cents),\n            )\n            return Budget(id=new_id, category_id=category_id, amount_cents=amount_cents)\n        self._db.execute(\n            \"UPDATE budgets SET amount_cents = ? WHERE id = ?\",\n            (amount_cents, existing.id),\n        )\n        return Budget(id=existing.id, category_id=category_id, amount_cents=amount_cents)\n\n    def find_by_category(self, category_id: int) -> Budget | None:\n        \"\"\"The budget of one category, or None when it has none.\"\"\"\n        rows = self._db.fetchall(\n            \"SELECT id, category_id, amount_cents FROM budgets WHERE category_id = ?\",\n            (category_id,),\n        )\n        if not rows:\n            return None\n        row = rows[0]\n        return Budget(\n            id=int(row[\"id\"]),\n            category_id=int(row[\"category_id\"]),\n            amount_cents=int(row[\"amount_cents\"]),\n        )\n\n    def list_all(self) -> list[Budget]:\n        \"\"\"Every stored budget, ordered by category.\"\"\"\n        rows = self._db.fetchall(\n            \"SELECT id, category_id, amount_cents FROM budgets ORDER BY category_id\"\n        )\n        return [\n            Budget(\n                id=int(row[\"id\"]),\n                category_id=int(row[\"category_id\"]),\n                amount_cents=int(row[\"amount_cents\"]),\n            )\n            for row in rows\n        ]\n\n\nclass CategoryRepository:\n    \"\"\"Reads the fixed category list and seeds it on first run.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, db: AppDatabase) -> None:\n        self._db = db\n\n    def list_all(self) -> list[Category]:\n        \"\"\"All categories in seed order.\"\"\"\n        rows = self._db.fetchall(\"SELECT id, name FROM categories ORDER BY id\")\n        return [Category(id=int(row[\"id\"]), name=str(row[\"name\"])) for row in rows]\n\n    def find_by_name(self, name: str) -> Category | None:\n        \"\"\"The category with this name (case-insensitive), or None.\"\"\"\n        rows = self._db.fetchall(\n            \"SELECT id, name FROM categories WHERE name = ? COLLATE NOCASE\",\n            (name,),\n        )\n        if not rows:\n            return None\n        row = rows[0]\n        return Category(id=int(row[\"id\"]), name=str(row[\"name\"]))\n\n    def seed_defaults(self) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Insert the seven fixed categories only when the table is empty.\"\"\"\n        if self.list_all():\n            return\n        for name in DEFAULT_CATEGORIES:\n            self._db.execute(\"INSERT INTO categories (name) VALUES (?)\", (name,))\n\n\n### expensetracker/server.py\n\"\"\"TrackerServer: the single-threaded local HTTP server.\n\nImplements the TrackerServer class of the domain class diagram and the\n\"Startup and storage\" sequence diagram.\nTrace: REQ-001\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nfrom http.server import BaseHTTPRequestHandler, HTTPServer\n\n\nclass TrackerServer:\n    \"\"\"Binds 127.0.0.1 and serves the tracker page and its JSON API.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, port: int, handler: type[BaseHTTPRequestHandler]) -> None:\n        self.port = port\n        self._httpd = HTTPServer((\"127.0.0.1\", port), handler)\n\n    def serve_forever(self) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Serve requests until the process is interrupted or shut down.\"\"\"\n        self._httpd.serve_forever()\n\n    def _bound_port(self) -> int:\n        \"\"\"The port actually in use (the OS picks one when 0 was requested).\"\"\"\n        return int(self._httpd.server_address[1])\n\n    def _shutdown(self) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Stop serving and release the socket.\"\"\"\n        self._httpd.shutdown()\n        self._httpd.server_close()\n\n\n### expensetracker/service.py\n\"\"\"ExpenseTrackerService: the use cases behind the JSON API.\n\nImplements the ExpenseTrackerService class of the domain class diagram and the\ncall order of the \"Log expense\", \"Set budget\", \"Budget overview\" and\n\"Monthly summary\" sequence diagrams.\nTrace: REQ-002, REQ-003, REQ-004, REQ-005, REQ-006, REQ-008, REQ-010\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nfrom datetime import datetime\n\nfrom .clock import Clock\nfrom .dates import Dates\nfrom .errors import ValidationError\nfrom .models import Budget, BudgetStatus, Category, Expense, MonthlySummary\nfrom .money import Money\nfrom .repositories import BudgetRepository, CategoryRepository, ExpenseRepository\n\n\ndef _split_month(month: str) -> tuple[int, int]:\n    \"\"\"Turn \"2026-05\" into (2026, 5).\"\"\"\n    try:\n        parsed = datetime.strptime(str(month), \"%Y-%m\")\n    except (TypeError, ValueError):\n        raise ValueError(f\"Invalid month {month!r}, expected YYYY-MM\") from None\n    return parsed.year, parsed.month\n\n\nclass ExpenseTrackerService:\n    \"\"\"Coordinates validation, repositories and the computed views.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(\n        self,\n        expenses: ExpenseRepository,\n        budgets: BudgetRepository,\n        categories: CategoryRepository,\n        clock: Clock,\n    ) -> None:\n        self._expenses = expenses\n        self._budgets = budgets\n        self._categories = categories\n        self._clock = clock\n\n    def add_expense(self, amount_text: str, date_text: str, category_name: str) -> Expense:\n        \"\"\"Validate the input, store the expense and return it with its new id.\"\"\"\n        amount_cents = Money.parse_amount(amount_text)\n        spent_on = Dates.parse_date(date_text)\n        category = self._require_category(category_name)\n        new_id = self._expenses.insert(\n            Expense(\n                id=0,\n                amount_cents=amount_cents,\n                spent_on=spent_on,\n                category_id=category.id,\n            )\n        )\n        return Expense(\n            id=new_id,\n            amount_cents=amount_cents,\n            spent_on=spent_on,\n            category_id=category.id,\n        )\n\n    def list_expenses(self) -> list[Expense]:\n        \"\"\"All recorded expenses, newest first.\"\"\"\n        return self._expenses.list_newest_first()\n\n    def set_budget(self, category_name: str, amount_text: str) -> Budget:\n        \"\"\"Validate the amount and store or update the category budget.\"\"\"\n        amount_cents = Money.parse_amount(amount_text)\n        category = self._require_category(category_name)\n        return self._budgets.upsert(category.id, amount_cents)\n\n    def budget_overview(self, month: str | None = None) -> list[BudgetStatus]:\n        \"\"\"Budget usage and warning level per budgeted category for one month.\"\"\"\n        target = month or self._clock.current_month()\n        year, month_number = _split_month(target)\n        spent = self._expenses.sum_by_category(year, month_number)\n        names = {category.id: category.name for category in self._categories.list_all()}\n        statuses: list[BudgetStatus] = []\n        for budget in self._budgets.list_all():\n            name = names.get(budget.category_id, \"Unknown\")\n            statuses.append(\n                BudgetStatus.evaluate(name, budget.amount_cents, spent.get(budget.category_id, 0))\n            )\n        return statuses\n\n    def monthly_summary(self, month: str | None = None) -> MonthlySummary:\n        \"\"\"Total and per-category spending of one calendar month.\"\"\"\n        target = month or self._clock.current_month()\n        year, month_number = _split_month(target)\n        spent = self._expenses.sum_by_category(year, month_number)\n        by_category: dict[str, int] = {}\n        total_cents = 0\n        for category in self._categories.list_all():\n            cents = spent.get(category.id, 0)\n            total_cents += cents\n            if cents:\n                by_category[category.name] = cents\n        return MonthlySummary(month=target, total_cents=total_cents, by_category=by_category)\n\n    def list_categories(self) -> list[Category]:\n        \"\"\"The fixed category list, in seed order.\"\"\"\n        return self._categories.list_all()\n\n    def _require_category(self, category_name: str) -> Category:\n        \"\"\"Resolve a category name to its row, or raise ValidationError(\"category\", ...).\"\"\"\n        text = \"\" if category_name is None else str(category_name).strip()\n        if not text:\n            raise ValidationError(\"category\", \"Category is required.\")\n        category = self._categories.find_by_name(text)\n        if category is None:\n            raise ValidationError(\"category\", f\"Unknown category {text!r}.\")\n        return category\n\n\n### expensetracker/static/app.js\n/*\n * TrackerPage: the browser view that talks to the local JSON API.\n * The same class exists as Python in expensetracker/page.py; this file is the\n * browser half of the TrackerPage view of the domain class diagram and\n * implements the renderer calls of the \"Log expense\", \"Budget overview\" and\n * \"Monthly summary\" sequence diagrams.\n * Trace: REQ-002, REQ-003, REQ-004, REQ-005, REQ-006, REQ-008, REQ-010\n */\n\nclass TrackerPage {\n  constructor() {\n    this.expenseForm = document.getElementById(\"expense-form\");\n    this.budgetForm = document.getElementById(\"budget-form\");\n    this.expenseRows = document.getElementById(\"expense-rows\");\n    this.expenseEmpty = document.getElementById(\"expense-empty\");\n    this.budgetRows = document.getElementById(\"budget-rows\");\n    this.budgetEmpty = document.getElementById(\"budget-empty\");\n    this.summaryTotal = document.getElementById(\"summary-total\");\n    this.summaryMonth = document.getElementById(\"summary-month\");\n    this.summaryCategories = document.getElementById(\"summary-categories\");\n    this.message = document.getElementById(\"message\");\n    this.categoryOptions = document.getElementById(\"expense-category\");\n    this.budgetCategoryOptions = document.getElementById(\"budget-category\");\n    this.dateInput = document.getElementById(\"expense-date\");\n  }\n\n  /** POST/GET JSON against the local server; resolves to {status, data}. */\n  async callApi(method, path, body) {\n    const options = { method: method, headers: {} };\n    if (body !== undefined && body !== null) {\n      options.headers[\"Content-Type\"] = \"application/json\";\n      options.body = JSON.stringify(body);\n    }\n    const response = await fetch(path, options);\n    let data = {};\n    try {\n      data = await response.json();\n    } catch (error) {\n      data = { message: \"The server sent an unexpected response.\" };\n    }\n    return { status: response.status, data: data };\n  }\n\n  /** Replace the expense table body with the given expenses (newest first). */\n  renderExpenses(expenses) {\n    this.expenseRows.replaceChildren();\n    if (!expenses || expenses.length === 0) {\n      this.expenseEmpty.hidden = false;\n      return;\n    }\n    this.expenseEmpty.hidden = true;\n    for (const expense of expenses) {\n      this.expenseRows.appendChild(this.buildRow(expense));\n    }\n  }\n\n  /** Insert one saved expense at its date position without refetching the list. */\n  insertRow(expense) {\n    this.expenseEmpty.hidden = true;\n    const row = this.buildRow(expense);\n    const rows = Array.from(this.expenseRows.querySelectorAll(\"tr\"));\n    const after = rows.find(function (existing) {\n      const date = existing.dataset.date || \"\";\n      if (date < expense.date) return true;\n      if (date > expense.date) return false;\n      return Number(existing.dataset.id || 0) < Number(expense.id || 0);\n    });\n    if (after) {\n      this.expenseRows.insertBefore(row, after);\n    } else {\n      this.expenseRows.appendChild(row);\n    }\n  }\n\n  buildRow(expense) {\n    const row = document.createElement(\"tr\");\n    row.dataset.date = expense.date;\n    row.dataset.id = expense.id;\n    for (const value of [expense.date, expense.category, expense.amount_display]) {\n      const cell = document.createElement(\"td\");\n      cell.textContent = value;\n      row.appendChild(cell);\n    }\n    const amountCell = row.lastElementChild;\n    amountCell.className = \"amount\";\n    return row;\n  }\n\n  /** Render each budgeted category with its usage and warning state. */\n  renderBudgets(statuses) {\n    this.budgetRows.replaceChildren();\n    if (!statuses || statuses.length === 0) {\n      this.budgetEmpty.hidden = false;\n      return;\n    }\n    this.budgetEmpty.hidden = true;\n    for (const status of statuses) {\n      const row = document.createElement(\"tr\");\n      row.dataset.category = status.category;\n      row.className = \"level-\" + String(status.level).toLowerCase();\n\n      const name = document.createElement(\"td\");\n      name.textContent = status.category;\n\n      const budget = document.createElement(\"td\");\n      budget.className = \"amount\";\n      budget.textContent = status.budget_display;\n\n      const spent = document.createElement(\"td\");\n      spent.className = \"amount\";\n      spent.textContent = status.spent_display;\n\n      const note = document.createElement(\"td\");\n      note.className = \"budget-message\";\n      note.textContent = status.message;\n      if (status.level !== \"OK\") {\n        const badge = document.createElement(\"span\");\n        badge.className = \"badge\";\n        badge.textContent = status.level === \"OVER\" ? \"Over budget\" : \"Close to limit\";\n        note.prepend(badge);\n      }\n\n      row.append(name, budget, spent, note);\n      this.budgetRows.appendChild(row);\n    }\n  }\n\n  /** Render the current month total and its per-category breakdown. */\n  renderSummary(summary) {\n    this.summaryMonth.textContent = summary.month || \"\";\n    this.summaryTotal.textContent = summary.total_display || \"0.00\";\n    this.summaryCategories.replaceChildren();\n    const categories = summary.categories || [];\n    if (categories.length === 0) {\n      const item = document.createElement(\"li\");\n      item.className = \"empty\";\n      item.textContent = \"No spending recorded this month yet.\";\n      this.summaryCategories.appendChild(item);\n      return;\n    }\n    for (const category of categories) {\n      const item = document.createElement(\"li\");\n      const name = document.createElement(\"span\");\n      name.textContent = category.name;\n      const value = document.createElement(\"span\");\n      value.className = \"amount\";\n      value.textContent = category.total_display;\n      item.append(name, value);\n      this.summaryCategories.appendChild(item);\n    }\n  }\n\n  /** Show a plain-language confirmation or validation message. */\n  showMessage(text, isError) {\n    this.message.textContent = text || \"\";\n    this.message.hidden = !text;\n    this.message.className = isError ? \"message error\" : \"message success\";\n    this.message.setAttribute(\"role\", isError ? \"alert\" : \"status\");\n  }\n\n  async loadCategories() {\n    const result = await this.callApi(\"GET\", \"/api/categories\");\n    const categories = (result.data && result.data.categories) || [];\n    for (const select of [this.categoryOptions, this.budgetCategoryOptions]) {\n      select.replaceChildren();\n      for (const category of categories) {\n        const option = document.createElement(\"option\");\n        option.value = category.name;\n        option.textContent = category.name;\n        select.appendChild(option);\n      }\n    }\n  }\n\n  async loadExpenses() {\n    const result = await this.callApi(\"GET\", \"/api/expenses\");\n    this.renderExpenses((result.data && result.data.expenses) || []);\n  }\n\n  async loadBudgets() {\